  "title": "Supporting Growth Through Connection",
  "content": "Connection is the foundation of healthy development. When children feel connected to their caregivers, they are more confident, more cooperative, and more resilient. Connection does not require perfection; it requires presence, warmth, and repair when things go wrong.\n\nThis lesson explores how everyday interactions—shared play, gentle touch, eye contact, and listening—shape a child’s emotional and cognitive growth. Connection strengthens the brain’s pathways for learning, empathy, and self‑regulation.\n\nParents learn how to use connection as a tool for guiding behaviour, reducing conflict, and supporting long‑term development.",
